  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    Plunge-Caller Oeichowei is the founder and leader of The Pinnacle, a splinter faction that broke from the Aurora Stack governing council Qingfu'spire over disputed trade-routes and mining rights. She is a cross-source magical practitioner of considerable and — from a taxonomic standpoint — deeply inconvenient ability, a veteran of combat against orca raiders, and a political operator whose methods are easier to document than to categorize cleanly as either principled or cynical. She emerged from The Promenade Ward, one of Aurora Stack's civic centers, during the Frozen Peace.
    
    ## Formation and Training
    
    Oeichowei trained in fire-channeling under Hainou mewei'Frostglass, an Aurora Stack merchant instrumental in the Promenade Ward's founding. She still visits Hainou in the deep tunnels — reportedly in secret, though enough sources mention it to question how secret it remains. Her flippers bear thin white scars where crystal shards worked their way out of her skin during early magic-work. The Mbra∴silentiu marks her as a survivor of an unspecified event she does not discuss. She wears Xueshei's Compass, a notable artifact, on a chain of aurora-glass.
    
    Her formal manner is Aurora Stack orthodoxy — astronomical metaphors, measured cadence — but multiple observers note a hesitation before certain terms, as if she is rendering something from a register that does not map neatly onto the Stack's vocabulary.
    
    ## The Schism
    
    Oeichowei drew The faceless Xi, a smuggler later blessed by the Radiant Aurora-harp at Light Ingjeizhi vault, and Cold-flip Qing from Qingfu'spire with promises of autonomy. The split occurred at The Aerie Perch, a crystal-spired trade post on the Berg's eastern reach. What the record preserves clearly is that Aishouwa the Frost-Bane — Oeichowei's closest ally and a formidable Aurora Stack warrior — stood silent when it happened, neither opposing nor endorsing. Oeichowei has never asked why. Aishouwa continues to follow her orders, carry her banner, and share rations. The silence between them on this point is, by all accounts, total.
    
    Oeichowei subsequently mandated that every Pinnacle member undergo a hearing of the Radiant Aurora-harp before swearing the faction's coded greeting — including members her own rationing mandates had previously condemned.
    
    ## Magical Practice
    
    Her source-training is aurora-light, but her practice of Hush☽ Twilight — a suppressive technique originating in Nightshelf ☽Silv-glaciere☽ Arts — draws from captured fire and pressure-depth. The Nightshelf observer Profundaea~ documented Oeichowei deploying suppressive silence during a trade-route dispute near the Radiant Aurora-harp, a surface location with no Nightshelf ice substrate. No protocol under Nightshelf hoarded-knowledge doctrine addresses an outsider carrying proprietary knowledge encoded in her own ice-memory, beyond retrieval or jurisdiction. The Office of Deep-Archive Provenance treatise on Hush☽ Twilight cites her case as evidence that the technique's propagation has rendered traditional classification untenable.
    
    ## Combat Record
    
    Her strike maimed the orca Rend Kzulrora, who later testified in Luminary Xuzhong Pelm'Oath's tribunal regarding events at the Drowned Ledge. The wound carries Oeichowei's name among orca pods — a distinction whose implications depend on whether one reads it as fear or grievance.
    
    ## Operational Methods
    
    During a Tide Custom festival at the Promenade Ward, Oeichowei positioned herself behind a crystal spire past the sightline of civic observers and gave a flipper-drop signal to Aishouwa — a command visible only at blade-level. This preceded the Frost-Bane's confrontation of a Nightshelf delegation over a contested artifact. Three mutually contradictory accounts of the resulting incident were filed without cross-examination.
